# mariadb-lsp-launcher — the extensionless name the plugin's config uses, so
# that ONE command works on macOS, Linux and native Windows alike: a JSON config
# cannot branch per OS, and Windows cannot run a .sh.
#
#   * On macOS and Linux the kernel runs THIS file through the shebang above,
#     and it hands over to mariadb-lsp-launcher.sh.
#   * On Windows, Claude Code and OpenCode resolve the command through
#     %PATHEXT% and land on mariadb-lsp-launcher.cmd next to it; this file,
#     having no extension, is not a program there. (Given a .sh command, they
#     run it through bash, which native Windows usually doesn't have on PATH.)
#
# The same device as Codex's mariadb-mcp-launcher. Verified on Windows 11
# ARM64 with Claude Code 2.1.306 and OpenCode 1.19.3.
exec "$(dirname "$0")/mariadb-lsp-launcher.sh" "$@"
